  <P STYLE="margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px; text-indent:4%"><FONT FACE="Times New Roman" SIZE="2">The model contains a proprietary concept that diversifies trading signals by time horizon. This type
of diversification is a principal component of the model and it allows clients to capture profit in the long-term. The model looks to participate in market movements and we have therefore devised a means of breaking down snap-shots of any market in
different time frames and we act on each time frame separately. </FONT></P>  <P STYLE="margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"><FONT SIZE="1">&nbsp;</FONT></P>  <P STYLE="margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px; text-indent:4%"><FONT
FACE="Times New Roman" SIZE="2">The model groups time parameters into short, medium and long-term trading signals; For example, the model&#146;s long-term view may be to sell, but the model may see an opportunity to <I>buy</I> in the short or
medium-term. The benefits of this are considerable. For example, by taking a multiple time frame view of any market, the fund doesn&#146;t concentrate on any one-time horizon (e.g. short term sentiment) but will take an equal view of all
opportunities presenting themselves in a market. </FONT></P>  <P STYLE="margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"><FONT SIZE="1">&nbsp;</FONT></P>  <P STYLE="margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"><FONT FACE="Times New Roman" SIZE="2"><B>Automated
Volatility Adjustment </B></FONT></P>  <P STYLE="margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:-6px"><FONT SIZE="1">&nbsp;</FONT></P>  <P STYLE="margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px; text-indent:4%"><FONT FACE="Times New Roman" SIZE="2">In order to capture
profits and adjust individual market positions according to market volatility the model incorporates another proprietary concept called the Volatility Adjustment Function. This function calculates short to medium term volatility for all assets
traded in the portfolio and adjusts the market positions for any change in volatility. This ensures that the required dollar volatility exposure is maintained in each market position and the risk taken in each market is totally controlled.
</FONT></P>  <P STYLE="margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"><FONT SIZE="1">&nbsp;</FONT></P>  <P STYLE="margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"><FONT FACE="Times New Roman" SIZE="2"><B>Asset Weighting and Leverage </B></FONT></P>  <P
STYLE="margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:-6px"><FONT SIZE="1">&nbsp;</FONT></P>  <P STYLE="margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px; text-indent:4%"><FONT FACE="Times New Roman" SIZE="2">The Horizon Program is designed to target a long-term annual volatility
of 15%. The portfolio is constructed so as to give each market sector an equal weighting. This ensures that no individual sector is favoured over another and that there is no bias due to historical performance. </FONT></P>  <P
STYLE="margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"><FONT SIZE="1">&nbsp;</FONT></P>  <P STYLE="margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"><FONT FACE="Times New Roman" SIZE="2"><B>The Team </B></FONT></P>  <P STYLE="margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:-6px"><FONT
SIZE="1">&nbsp;</FONT></P>  <P STYLE="margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px; text-indent:4%"><FONT FACE="Times New Roman" SIZE="2">The system has been developed by Sanjeev Lakhanpal, Dr Paul Netherwood and Alan Goulding. The team have over 40 years of
fund management and investment banking experience between them including experience with Credit Suisse First Boston, Nomura and Deutsche Bank. The team originally met when they were part of the trading, research and development team at AHL (now ED
&amp; F Man Investment Products). On joining Beach they embarked on building a system and a model that was a radical improvement on the automated systems witnessed from their collective experience to date. The Horizon Program is the result of that
