born in 1959, joined C-View in May 2001 and is a Director at C-View. Prior to joining C-View, he was at Dresdner Kleinwort Wasserstein, London, where he ran Foreign Exchange Proprietary Trading from 1998 to 2001. Mr. Eesteren started his financial
career at Salomon Brothers (formerly Philipp Brothers) in New York, and then became a Senior Proprietary Trader and Global Head of Currency Options at the Bank of America, London, New York and Tokyo. He then became an Executive Director and Senior
Proprietary trader at the Union Bank of Switzerland, London and afterwards joined Nationsbank in Chicago and London as a Senior Proprietary Trader and Senior Vice President. Mr. Van Eesteren holds a Masters Degree of International Management from
&#145;Thunderbird&#146;, Graduate School of International Management and a Bachelor of Arts from the University of Pudget Sound, completing three years of studies at Nijenrode, the Netherlands School of Business. </FONT></P>  <P
STYLE="margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"><FONT SIZE="1">&nbsp;</FONT></P> <P STYLE="margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:2%"><FONT FACE="Times New Roman" SIZE="2"><I>Mark A. Clarke </I></FONT></P> <P
STYLE="margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:-6px"><FONT SIZE="1">&nbsp;</FONT></P>  <P STYLE="margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px; text-indent:4%"><FONT FACE="Times New Roman" SIZE="2">Mr. Clarke, born in 1964, is a senior trader and about to become a
Principal of C-View. Mr. Clarke has been actively trading foreign exchange for the past 16 years and began his trading career in 1986, specializing in spot USD/JPY at Bank of America. Mr. Clarke was a high profile and extremely successful trader,
being recruited by several top houses including UBS and First Chicago to both trade and build their foreign exchange business during the late 1980&#146;s and 1990&#146;s. Prior to joining C-View in 2002, Mr. Clarke worked at Credit Agricole Indosuez
(&#147;CAI&#148;) in London for 6 years where he was globally responsible for foreign exchange trading. Mr.&nbsp;Clarke was instrumental in shaping CAI&#146;s e-commerce platform and sat on the board of FXall. Mr. Clarke graduated <I>summa cum
laude</I> in 1986, with a B.Sc. (Hon) Business Economics from the University of Wales. </FONT></P>  <P STYLE="margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"><FONT SIZE="1">&nbsp;</FONT></P> <P STYLE="margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:2%"><FONT
FACE="Times New Roman" SIZE="2"><I>Quinn Joseph Hebert </I></FONT></P> <P STYLE="margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:-6px"><FONT SIZE="1">&nbsp;</FONT></P>  <P STYLE="margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px; text-indent:4%"><FONT FACE="Times New Roman"
SIZE="2">Mr. Herbert, born in 1963, is a director at C-View. He was a corporate associate at the law firm of Jones, Walker, Waechter, Poitevent, Carrere and Denegre law firm in New Orleans, Louisiana from 1988 to 1993. He handled general corporate
advices and various mergers and acquisitions transactions including initial public offerings, debt offerings and various financial restructuring transactions. Thereafter he joined Ceanic Corporation (formerly American Oilfield Divers, Inc.), or
Ceanic, in Houston, Texas., as a V.P. and General Counsel from 1993 to 1998. While at Ceanic, he was a member of a four person Executive Committee responsible for the strategic direction of company. Ceanic was acquired by Stolt Comex Seaway S.A., or
SCS, in August 1998. From November 1998 to the present, Mr. Hebert served as the President and CEO for SCS&#146;s North Americas Region, where he handles the traditional duties of President/CEO and is responsible for profit and loss of USD$200
million plus annual revenues, 1,000 plus full time employees and USD$175 million of operating assets. </FONT></P>  <P STYLE="margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"><FONT SIZE="1">&nbsp;</FONT></P> <P
STYLE="margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px; text-indent:4%"><FONT FACE="Times New Roman" SIZE="2">Mr. Herbert received his B.A., <I>summa cum laude, </I>from Louisiana State University in 1985 and a Juris Doctor from Boston College Law School in May
1988. While at Boston College Law School, he was the Executive Editor of the Boston College International and Comparative Law Review. Mr. Herbert is admitted to practice law in the State of Louisiana and is a member of American Bar Association and
the American Corporate Counsel Association. </FONT></P> <P STYLE="margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"><FONT SIZE="1">&nbsp;</FONT></P>
